"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026","html_url":"https://github.com/Nexus-os2026","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/actions/runs/37163435032/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/actions/runs/37163435032/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/check-suites/100664377547","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/actions/runs/37163435032/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/actions/runs/37163435032/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/actions/runs/37163435032/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexus-os2026/nexus-os/actions/workflows/371750689","head_commit":{"id":"d16d7ca30e9f6431c9399e6facd4bda26b4a1740","tree_id":"ea97059154e91d9879838ef78b2e38d0431bcfd9","message":"fix(verifier): bind candidate cleanup ownership\n\nP2-V1-R3B-I4-R3-R1 stops a pending scope operation from ending a cgroup\nmerely because the kernel reports the helper in it. On the base (44a4fc6c)\nacquire() and the proof opened the cgroup of the unit's name the helper\nwas in and killed it at once, and an uncertain start was proven like an\naccepted one: a lost UnitExists whose foreign cgroup held the helper and a\nprocess of its own was opened, proven, launched into and that process\nended, and a same-name replacement that took the helper was ended, and\nproven while the proof waited (reproduced on the base's own model and\nproduction code: reproduction/before-repair.out).\n\n- Identity (primary sources, systemd 255.4-1ubuntu8.17 and v255.4):\n  InvocationID is a fresh random 128-bit value per start, never settable\n  by a caller. An accepted start captures the identity of the invocation\n  it began from its own job: Subscribe, then JobRemoved for the job and\n  the unit's PropertiesChanged matched before the request is sent; among\n  the reply sender's changes with serials strictly between the reply and\n  the job's removal (done), exactly one distinct 16-byte identity\n  (captured_instance). Nothing else yields one.\n- Three states: an observed candidate (retained descriptor, no authority:\n  never ended, never proven, its emptiness confirms nothing); an owned\n  candidate, bound to the captured invocation (the helper at the\n  descriptor's path; InvocationID, Id, ControlGroup, the directory's own\n  kernel cgroup ID as ControlGroupId, InvocationID again): the only\n  cgroup.kill of a pending operation; the proven scope, an owned candidate\n  whose limits, runtime backstop and out-of-memory policy are proven, the\n  identity read again: the only launch. A policy failure after ownership\n  refuses the launch and ends the owned candidate.\n- An uncertain start never opens, owns, ends, proves or confirms anything\n  (accepted availability cost); an accepted start without a captured\n  identity is confirmed only by the manager's absence; a delivered\n  UnitExists is unchanged. Nothing acts on a unit by its name.\n- Production: scope/pending.rs, scope/manager.rs, scope.rs (the Scope\n  holds its invocation; harness-only read accessors), fault.rs (two fault\n  points), and scope/native.rs (a descriptor's kernel cgroup ID by file\n  handle), which is outside the mission's listed files and surfaced in\n  the evidence.\n- Tests over the deterministic model: r3r1_01 to r3r1_11 and r3r1_x_*\n  (153 lib tests, from 138); the model gains unit identities, directory\n  IDs, the capture through the production rule, interference and new\n  panic points; four tests renamed, their old names stating what is now\n  forbidden (listed in the evidence).\n- Controls: eleven R3-R1 mutation controls. The accepted runners and R3's\n  adapters rerun unchanged (SHA-256 verified), the first unadapted run\n  kept; R3-R1 adapters re-anchor or re-express what R3-R1 moved (R3 7, R2\n  4, Q1-R1 1, I4/I4-R1 10, API guards 2, source guards 5 adapted plus one\n  guard added), each with its reason; Q1 unadapted.\n- Live: the H3/H4 case reads InvocationID (ay, 16 bytes) against the\n  identity production recorded and ControlGroupId against the retained\n  descriptor; built, never run; the count stays 39.\n\nNo dependency, Cargo.lock, custody, workflow or live-count change. The live\nharness was built, never run: the runner's user manager is still absent\n(run 37091121444); nothing was provisioned or dispatched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N5tKJB1n4kYCCSym5GnaZY","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:19:55Z","author":{"name":"Suresh Karicheti","email":"nexaiceo@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"Suresh Karicheti","email":"nexaiceo@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1186727446,"node_id":"R_kgDORrwGFg","name":"nexus-os","full_name":"Nexus-os2026/nexus-os","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Nexus-os2026","id":269544206,"node_id":"U_kgDOEBDrDg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269544206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026","html_url":"https://github.com/Nexus-os2026","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexus-os2026/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/